<title>HUNGARY: TVK initiates repayment of HUF 5 bln.</title>
<headline>TVK initiates repayment of HUF 5 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarian chemicals firm TVK said on Thursday it had initiated with the state privatisation agency APV Rt the repayment of five billion forints to the company's accounts.</p>
<p>The amount, which sparked enormous turnover and once again new record price for TVK shares on Thursday, stems from the company's privatisation and is based on Hungary's previous privatisation law, it said in the official bourse gazette.</p>
<p>On Wednesday TVK shares rallied to a new record of 1,855 forints after a report by daily Napi Gazdasag breaking the news.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
